# ========================= Hackathon compute config (ONE place) =========================
# Copy to `compute.env` (same dir) and fill it in. Every project reads it through
# poseidon_compute. compute.env is gitignored — never commit your keys.

# --- Inference: set at least ONE key — Nebius AI Studio and OpenRouter are interchangeable --------
# Both are OpenAI-compatible; the client uses whichever key you provide. Nebius serves open models;
# OpenRouter additionally covers closed ones (GPT/Gemini/Claude). Set the one you have credits for
# (or both). `poseidon-run` sends your chosen model to whichever of them serves it, and only falls
# back to hosting it on Modal if neither does.
NEBIUS_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: FORCE one model for EVERY project and EVERY role (an exact Nebius / Hugging Face model id).
# WARNING: this overrides whatever model the code asks for, everywhere. It therefore COLLAPSES
# multi-model experiments — e.g. trace-guard's trusted-vs-untrusted monitor, and llm-agent-collusion(-2)'s
# rosters / judges / overseers — into a single model, which invalidates their comparison. Leave it UNSET
# for those; use a per-run `--model` or the experiment's own model flags instead. When set, the override
# is announced at runtime. If you pick a model Nebius doesn't serve, run via `poseidon-run` (OpenRouter ->
# Modal -> fail; nothing is silently substituted).
# LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct
